From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: chelovechishee <261262090+chelovechishee@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH 36/43] arm64: dts: exynos7885: the ALIVE wakeup EINT mux is
 SPI 16

gpa0 and gpa1 have one GIC interrupt per pin (SPI 0-15); the other
wakeup banks (gpa2, gpq0) share one more, SPI 16 in the vendor device
tree. SPI 130 named here belongs to the DISPAUD pin controller, so no
interrupt of gpa2 or gpq0 ever arrived: on the Galaxy Tab A 10.1 the
S2MU005 charger (gpa2-2) only set its currents once, at probe.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7885.dtsi | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7885.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7885.dtsi
index 4f137dcfa..4a71882fe 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7885.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7885.dtsi
@@ -601,7 +601,8 @@ wakeup-interrupt-controller {
 				compatible = "samsung,exynos7885-wakeup-eint",
 					     "samsung,exynos7-wakeup-eint";
 				interrupt-parent = <&gic>;
-				interrupts = <GIC_SPI 130 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+				/* gpa2 and gpq0 (gpa0/gpa1 have one SPI per pin) */
+				interrupts = <GIC_SPI 16 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
 			};
 		};
 
